WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:04.230
A wedding canopy: four
poles, open at the sides.

2
00:00:04.280 --> 00:00:06.230
A couple stands beneath it.

3
00:00:06.280 --> 00:00:09.300
At the very end, the
groom stamps on a glass.

4
00:00:09.350 --> 00:00:12.190
It shatters, and the guests cheer.

5
00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:13.740
Now a funeral.

6
00:00:13.790 --> 00:00:16.820
Close relatives tear a
garment they are wearing.

7
00:00:16.870 --> 00:00:19.460
Why would a wedding end
with breaking a glass,

8
00:00:19.510 --> 00:00:22.340
and mourning begin with tearing clothes?

9
00:00:22.390 --> 00:00:26.060
In this mission, you'll follow
a Jewish wedding step by step,

10
00:00:26.110 --> 00:00:29.040
from the marriage contract
to the seven blessings.

11
00:00:29.090 --> 00:00:32.400
Then you'll trace how Jewish
mourning moves in stages,

12
00:00:32.450 --> 00:00:35.470
from the day of death through
the weeks that follow.

13
00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:40.250
Your mission: find out why a Jewish
wedding ends by smashing a glass,

14
00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:42.680
and mourning begins by tearing a shirt.
